              "text": "vindicō, vindicāre — \"to claim; to avenge, to punish\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Iniūriam vindicāvit. He avenged the wrong."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "vindicō, vindicāre, vindicāvī, vindicātum. In law, to claim a thing as one's own; in lībertātem vindicāre, to set free. English vindicate."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
